WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.135 line:0%
-It's in the cloud.
It's in the cloud.

00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:06.972 line:0%
O.J.! It's in the cloud!

00:00:06.972 --> 00:00:08.775 line:0%
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:15.614 --> 00:00:17.583 line:0%
-Yeah, naw, naw, naw.

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:20.153 line:0%
Run, O.J.! Run!

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:27.727
♪♪

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:35.267
♪♪

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:37.603
-Welcome back to "Late Night,"
everybody.

00:00:37.603 --> 00:00:39.071
We're here with Daniel Kaluuya,

00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:41.241
Keke Palmer, Brandon Perea,
Director Jordan Peele.

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:43.042
That was a clip from "Nope."

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:44.777
It's about all you want
to see in a clip.

00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:46.645
I feel like you don't want
to see much more.

00:00:46.645 --> 00:00:49.348
Because this is not a movie
you want spoiled

00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:51.317
before you actually go
to the theater.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.052
"Nope" is a wonderful title.

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:54.620
How -- When did you
come up with it?

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.388
And did you know
when you came up with it

00:00:56.388 --> 00:00:58.124
that you had a winner?

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.626
-I mean, it was pretty late.

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:04.130
I was -- I wrote the movie
with a different title in mind.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.665
I had different things
I was trying out.

00:01:06.665 --> 00:01:09.468
When I hit "Nope," it just made
sense because the movie,

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:12.604
it just -- it's not even a --
it's like a concept.

00:01:12.604 --> 00:01:14.407
You know,
it's one of those films

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:18.611
that I think just sort of
needs its own type of title.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.446
So, yeah, yeah, I knew.

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:22.415
-I remember when he talked
about it with us both,

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:23.882
and I was like, "That's it!"

00:01:23.882 --> 00:01:25.584
Do you remember that?
-No, I do not remember.

00:01:25.584 --> 00:01:27.586
[ Laughter ]
I don't remember one bit.

00:01:27.586 --> 00:01:30.056
I was like, "'Nope' is amazing.
'Nope' is amazing."

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:32.325
And another time Keke was like,
"I like that one!"

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:34.828
-No, I didn't --

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:36.362
[ Talking over each other ]

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.998
-That's a lie.
-Don't tell --

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:42.034
Don't tell the secrets.

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:43.569
-I didn't know that it was
called "Nope."

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:46.105
And then I saw it, like,
on the action clapper board.

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:47.873
And I was like, "Oh, he's not
revealing the title yet."

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:49.542
I just did not know
it was "Nope."

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.277
And then I heard...

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:53.979
-Yeah, every day,
they go to Jordan

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:55.314
and they're like, "Did you
come up with a title yet?"

00:01:55.314 --> 00:01:57.584
-And he would say, "Nope."

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:59.618
-Eventually they just
started putting it down.

00:01:59.618 --> 00:02:01.454
-Yeah. And it worked out.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.455
So, you -- We talked about this.

00:02:03.455 --> 00:02:04.924
You are a huge horror fan.

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:09.695
But, also, do you believe
in the sort of extraterrestrial?

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:11.297
-Absolutely without a doubt.
-Okay.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.599
-Come on. You've got to believe
there's something out there.

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:16.469
They could be out there.
-Okay.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:18.637
Do not besmirch my audience.

00:02:18.637 --> 00:02:20.305
[ Laughter ]
-But they're cool.

00:02:20.305 --> 00:02:21.908
They're not blowing us up, man.
-Yeah, that's true.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:23.443
They've been here
the whole night.

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:27.247
We can't give them a hard time.
Now, you -- I heard that you --

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:30.783
The existence of koalas informs
how you feel about aliens.

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.553
-Yeah, because koalas exist.

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:36.522
So if there's a koala, there's
got to be something up there.

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:39.526
It's like kangaroos.
There's Chihuahuas.

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:41.627
They're, like,
weird-looking animals.

00:02:41.627 --> 00:02:43.763
If you really look,
they're very weird,

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:45.264
and they've got weird names.

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:47.166
So then, you think, what,
in Jupiter, they ain't got,

00:02:47.166 --> 00:02:51.404
like, a koala --
like, a koala going...

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:53.739
I just think, like -- Yeah.

00:02:53.739 --> 00:02:55.675
If there's kangaroos,
there have got to be aliens.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:58.077
-Okay. Gotcha.
That's a very --

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:01.581
I respect the science
behind this decision.

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:04.049
Jordan gave you
some film assignments.

00:03:04.049 --> 00:03:05.518
-Yeah.
-This was --

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.686
What were some of the movies
he wanted you to watch, Brandon?

00:03:07.686 --> 00:03:10.223
-So, the film list that I got
on the day I got the job

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:12.025
was "Close Encounters
of the Third Kind,"

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:14.527
"Jaws," "2001: A Space Odyssey,"

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.395
"Alien,"
and "No Country For Old Men."

00:03:16.395 --> 00:03:19.032
And I was like,
"What does this mean?"

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:20.800
And I -- So, I took the job

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.534
without knowing what the heck
the movie was about.

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:24.236
There was no synopsis released.

00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:25.671
A month and a half later,

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:28.574
I get a text message from Peele
on Christmas Day

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:30.509
just being like,
"Merry Christmas."

00:03:30.509 --> 00:03:31.844
And it was the script.

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.546
So I accepted the job
not knowing what I was doing,

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:34.780
but I was like,
"It's Jordan Peele.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.281
I'm going to do whatever
he wants me to do."

00:03:36.281 --> 00:03:37.983
And then I read the script,
and I was just floored.

00:03:37.983 --> 00:03:39.352
-I know.

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:41.087
-I gave them some movies
to watch because I had to stall.

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:43.789
I had to rewrite the script.
-He did.

00:03:43.789 --> 00:03:44.957
-I had to figure it out.

00:03:44.957 --> 00:03:46.425
-Yeah, some of those
are very long movies.

00:03:46.425 --> 00:03:48.661
I noticed.
-Very long movies.

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:50.996
I was ready to add some.

00:03:50.996 --> 00:03:56.035
Yeah, but -- You know,
I do believe in UFOs.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:58.204
I'm just -- I want to say that.

00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:00.272
Or I believe in aliens.

00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:04.743
And I believe in life
that is not us in this universe.

00:04:04.743 --> 00:04:08.814
And I -- Sometimes I think
if aliens came down, like,

00:04:08.814 --> 00:04:10.283
I would turn on all of y'all.

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:12.151
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:14.454
-Oh, interesting.
-Like in a heartbeat.

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:18.323
And it's not -- It's not
because I don't like you.

00:04:18.323 --> 00:04:20.325
But I feel like

00:04:20.325 --> 00:04:23.963
there might be room
for, like, one prime human

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:26.432
on the alien...
-So he made a movie.

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:27.666
-And so I made a movie.

00:04:27.666 --> 00:04:29.234
I would make that move
is all I'm saying.

00:04:29.234 --> 00:04:31.237
I don't --

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:32.805
-So you basically made a movie

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:34.807
that you would have to show them
if it ever happened.

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:36.809
-I just don't know --
If there's aliens out there,

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.677
I already don't know
whose side I'm on.

00:04:38.677 --> 00:04:40.179
That's all I'm saying.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.648
-That's very honest of you
to come right out and say it.

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:44.917
So, Keke, I've heard
that you based your character,

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.619
Emerald, on a couple
of people --

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:50.290
Marty McFly from "Back
to the Future" and your dad.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:52.725
-Yeah!
-Here's your dad right there.

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:54.694
-My dad's the best.
-Is that premiere night?

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:56.262
-Literally
that's premiere night.

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:57.496
-Alright. That's great.

00:04:57.496 --> 00:04:59.064
-And I love his little outfit,
his little tie.

00:04:59.064 --> 00:05:00.466
My dad is the sweetest man
in the world.

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:03.302
And I really did --
I admired my dad all growing up.

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:05.771
And my character, she's so cool
and confident in who she is.

00:05:05.771 --> 00:05:08.274
And she also admired her brother
and her dad.

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:11.243
And so I just felt like,
"Yeah, let's pull from that."

00:05:11.243 --> 00:05:14.213
-That's a nice way to pull from.
Daniel, I've talked on the show

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:17.049
that my parents give me feedback
on everything I do.

00:05:17.049 --> 00:05:18.417
They watch every show.

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:20.786
I have no complaints,
but they do give me notes.

00:05:20.786 --> 00:05:23.122
I've heard your mom
does the same.

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:27.459
-She gives me notes, yeah.
A lot of notes. A lot of notes.

00:05:27.459 --> 00:05:29.561
-The difference is, you know,
I've got a show tomorrow night.

00:05:29.561 --> 00:05:32.098
So, like, they can give me notes
and I can fix it the next night.

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:33.899
But, like, the movie's done.

00:05:33.899 --> 00:05:37.036
-I know, so it's not --
I can't do anything about it.

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:38.203
"That wasn't..."

00:05:38.203 --> 00:05:40.405
"I can't --
I can't reshoot that now.

00:05:40.405 --> 00:05:42.108
It's released."

00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:44.109
-But do you like it?
I mean, obviously, it comes

00:05:44.109 --> 00:05:45.845
from a place
of love and support, right?

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:47.379
-Yeah, it's --
She's actually told me

00:05:47.379 --> 00:05:49.715
not to talk about her
in public anymore.

00:05:49.715 --> 00:05:52.785
She's like, "No, don't do that,
don't do that."

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:56.055
But I asked her about "Nope"
and she said, "No comment."

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:57.089
-Really?!
-Yeah.

00:05:57.089 --> 00:05:59.091
-That doesn't --
-I'll speak to you later.

00:05:59.091 --> 00:06:01.093
-I'll speak to you later.
-I'll speak to you later.

00:06:01.093 --> 00:06:02.561
-She doesn't want
you exposing her.

00:06:02.561 --> 00:06:03.996
She doesn't want you
exposing her.

00:06:03.996 --> 00:06:06.232
-She knows what I'm like.
Do it after the press run.

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:07.433
-Oh, I see, right.

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:08.734
-Early September,
I'll get reviewed.

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:10.302
-There you go.

00:06:10.302 --> 00:06:11.837
Brandon,
you have a special skill

00:06:11.837 --> 00:06:13.339
that did not turn up
in the film.

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:15.674
But this is an incredible
piece of trivia

00:06:15.674 --> 00:06:18.644
about you
that I found out today.

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:24.183
You were the youngest
professional roller skater --

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:25.518
-That break-dances
on roller skates.

00:06:25.518 --> 00:06:27.386
Yeah, so I turned pro
at the youngest age.

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:29.654
I think I turned pro
at 14 years old.

00:06:29.654 --> 00:06:30.990
No one has done that.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:33.626
I mean, break-dancing
on roller skates is very --

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:34.761
It's a tiny sport.

00:06:34.761 --> 00:06:37.096
People play ping-pong
on a tennis court

00:06:37.096 --> 00:06:38.598
far more than they break-dance
in roller skates.

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:40.032
-Okay, gotcha.
-So it's a very niche thing.

00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:42.568
-So you were a professional
break-dancing roller skater?

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:43.936
-Yeah.
-Okay, got[ Chatter ].

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:45.938
-Yeah, so I --
-I love it.

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:47.707
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:47.707 --> 00:06:50.476
-So, I can do some things.
I can do some things.

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:52.845
-We were actually -- We heard
that you could do a backflip.

00:06:52.845 --> 00:06:54.947
-Yeah, I can do a backflip.
-But we were also told --

00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:56.516
When I asked the producer,
they said,

00:06:56.516 --> 00:06:58.150
"Don't let him
because of insurance."

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:00.319
-It's fine. It's fine.
-And I shouldn't say this,

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:02.254
but our cue-card guy
already fell today.

00:07:02.254 --> 00:07:04.356
-Oh, no.
-Are you alright?

00:07:04.356 --> 00:07:07.093
-Is that him over there?
-Yeah, he's alright.

00:07:07.093 --> 00:07:09.629
-Are you from --
-Yeah, that's Wally.

00:07:09.629 --> 00:07:12.131
Don't take your mask off, Wally.

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:16.502
"Oh, the 'SNL' host knows me.
I got to take my mask off."

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:18.804
-There's video clips,
so I can prove it.

00:07:18.804 --> 00:07:21.106
-Alright. Everybody can go
watch video clips

00:07:21.106 --> 00:07:23.642
of Brandon
where we are not at liability.

00:07:23.642 --> 00:07:25.711
So please watch
and enjoy those.

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:29.215
And we will be right back with
more "Late Night," everybody.

